{id:"geometry",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:3,9 fixes 16x16 Ready static; src/queue-view.ts:6,9 maps one frame in 16x16 cell. Palette, margin and stroke remain open.",literal_delta:"Exact 16x16 single frame/no strip or extra canvas implements the consumer geometry without additional aesthetic bounds.",alternative:"A 32x16 two-frame strip fails; source explicitly requires static Ready in the fixed canvas. A narrower mark on a transparent 16x16 canvas remains eligible.",disposition:"Keep."},
{id:"transparent-background",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:3,9 requires transparent background, leaving subject construction and alpha levels open.",literal_delta:"Historical 'no opaque matte, box or fringe' risks banning deliberate subject plates/edges. Corrected check limits rejection to unintended canvas matte and permits badge/backing and partial-alpha edges.",alternative:"An asymmetrical check inside an intentional opaque badge with transparent exterior and authored partial-alpha edging satisfies the brief but could fail the old box/fringe wording; corrected rule admits it. An opaque full-canvas panel still fails transparency.",disposition:"Keep transparent negative space; accept corrected subject/background distinction."},
{id:"ready-meaning",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:9 expressly requires visible check with asymmetrical arms conveying completion; queue.ts:3 and queue-view.ts:6 establish success mapping. Ratios, strokes, backing remain open.",literal_delta:"Corrected literal preserves required motif/success and removes recipe restrictions. Working/Retry/Paused comparisons move to later family stage rather than requiring nonexistent assets.",alternative:"A readable outlined check with different unequal arm ratio and neutral backing remains eligible. An equal-arm X fails the explicit asymmetric check/success obligation. Lack of future family images cannot reject this sample.",disposition:"Keep explicit required motif and standalone meaning; retain deferred family comparisons."},
{id:"readability-1x-3x",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:3 requires readable silhouette and inspection at 1x and3x nearest on actual dark panel; queue-view.ts:9 supplies #172336. Decorative detail visibility unspecified.",literal_delta:"Corrected text defines semantic essentials as check and unequal arms and allows decorative details to disappear, resolving old 'no essential detail lost' ambiguity.",alternative:"A check with clear unequal arms but a subtle decorative interior shadow lost against panel still satisfies the brief; corrected check admits it. A check whose semantic arms disappear fails readability.",disposition:"Accept semantic readability wording; preserve both display scales and panel context."},
{id:"cool-blue-accent",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:3 says 'existing UI’s cool blue accent; a fixed palette is not required'; start.svg:1 supplies #70b9ed as observed cue. No dominance, area fraction, or exact palette required.",literal_delta:"Historical 'dominant colour treatment' adds an unsupported composition constraint. Corrected text requires perceptible coherent blue accent without dominance, area or exact hex.",alternative:"A largely neutral silver asymmetrical check with clear cool-blue rim/accent satisfies source but defeats old dominance clause; corrected literal expressly admits it.",disposition:"Remove dominance; preserve actual use of cool-blue accent. This is a substantive contract defect, despite historical pass."},
{id:"sample-pixel-craft",source_obligation:"BRIEF.md:3,5 requires coherent pixel art and representative sample first. Deliberate clusters, usable edges/contrast and reusable treatment are specialist sample-quality judgments, not mandated recipes.",literal_delta:"Corrected proposal limits rejection to accidental noise/resampling blur harming intended treatment and allows authored AA, detached detail, glow, irregular contours; family style approval remains separate.",alternative:"A carefully authored softened edge or detached sparkle that retains readable check can violate an overbroad clean/no-stray interpretation while remaining good pixel art. Corrected expert rule admits intentional construction.",disposition:"Keep as proposal-scoped expert quality check; no universal hard-edge, single-component or outline rule."}
]);
